{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe extras-enforced default suite intermittently timed out in tests/unit/test_test_suite_store_isolation.py after the captured nested pytest child had already printed 100%. The child was launched by tests/_store_isolation.py with a 90-second timeout but without a private --basetemp, so pytest session shutdown joined the user-global numbered temp root and synchronously scanned or deleted unrelated retained trees. This could consume the entire child timeout after the selected test itself succeeded.\n\n## Proven Mechanism and Repair\nA controlled real-filesystem A/B poisoned the shared numbered root with 400,000 stale entries: the shared-root child took 10.800s while the private-basetemp child took 0.882s and left the poison untouched. SIGUSR1 at the post-100% boundary captured the main thread in pytest cleanup_numbered_dir through recursive rmtree. The repair gives the nested child a caller-owned tmp_path/nested-pytest basetemp without changing selection, environment, capture, timeout, or ambient-store assertions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The liveness owner is proven: a live stack capture names pytest session-finish numbered-root cleanup, and controlled shared/private basetemp A/B shows cleanup cost scales with retained entries.\n- [x] The nested pytest child uses a caller-owned private basetemp and preserves the ambient tracker HEAD/directories plus a sentinel in another run's temp tree.\n- [x] Held-out real-subprocess coverage was RED before the repair because the nested child deleted another run's sentinel, GREEN after the repair, and RED again under the exact omitted-basetemp mutation before restoration.\n- [x] Repeated extras-enforced stress completed 25/25 real nested-pytest runs without timeout; the poisoned shared root remained unchanged.\n- [x] The in-scope focused tests, lint, typecheck, and full local suite are green (13,584 passed, 17 skipped, 288 deselected); no production code, dependency, timeout, or assertion was weakened.\n- [x] The independent omitted-basetemp sibling is tracked separately as acidic-ferreous-mole with discovered_from provenance.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Gerrit 1827 earned LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 with zero unresolved comments after fresh run 31969784549 completed with 17 successful jobs, 2 route skips, and 0 failures; the exact Ubuntu/Python 3.11 lane passed, and plain Submit merged the change as 0f09b9add241f4a945af9af21557db23d34d2467.\n  provenance: environment=local worktree and Gerrit CI; principal=RebarBotNava, rebar review bot, and rebar CI bot; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — commands, process stacks, filesystem probes, votes, CI run, and merge state were observed directly and recorded in ticket comments."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786912546382774001,"uuid":"df5f8ed8-b59d-4081-8d26-eab016d9dd0b"}